# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 77-81 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): the holy things carried (77), the altar (78),
# observe and hear (79), the nations cut off (80), the snare and the abomination (81) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch12_ink.SP_; the
# middah where the row argues by one (checked). Chapter 11's form.
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(77, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONLY YOUR HOLY THINGS WHICH YOU HAVE, AND YOUR VOWS, YOU SHALL TAKE UP AND GO TO THE PLACE" (12:26) — OF WHAT DOES THE VERSE SPEAK? IF OF THE HOLY THINGS OF THE LAND — IT IS SAID; IT SPEAKS ONLY OF THE HOLY THINGS OF OUTSIDE THE LAND. The head row of piska 77 ({SP_(77, 1, "בקדשי", "חוצה", "לארץ")} "of the holy things of outside the Land"): the verse assigned by elimination to consecrated animals from abroad (a PARAMETER of origin); Onkelos supplies "the tithe of" your holy things (the ink) — a second assignment. Fresh; Temurah 21a at 10b.')
srow(77, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU SHALL TAKE UP AND GO" — HE IS BOUND TO THE CARE OF BRINGING THEM UNTIL THE CHOSEN HOUSE; R. JUDAH: UNTIL THE WELL OF THE EXILE HE IS RESPONSIBLE, FROM THERE ON NOT. ({SP_(77, 2, "עד", "באר", "הגולה", "חיב", "באחריותם")} "until the Well of the Exile he is responsible for them"): Tosefta Bikkurim 1:5 (the English\'s note on the well); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(77, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT EVEN THE FIRSTBORN AND THE TITHE? "YOUR VOWS" — HOLY THINGS THAT COME BY VOW AND FREEWILL; THE FIRSTBORN AND THE TITHE, WHICH DO NOT, ARE OUT. ({SP_(77, 3, "יצאו", "בכור", "ומעשר")} "the firstborn and the tithe went out"): "your vows" a restriction — the responsibility a PARAMETER by the offering\'s kind. Fresh.')
srow(77, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT I EXCLUDE THE SIN AND GUILT OFFERING? "YOUR HOLY THINGS." ({SP_(77, 4, "תלמוד", "לומר", "קדשיך")} "the Teaching states: your holy things"). Fresh.')
srow(77, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'WHAT MOVED YOU TO INCLUDE THE SIN AND GUILT AND EXCLUDE THE FIRSTBORN AND TITHE? AFTER INCLUDING, THE VERSE RESTRICTED: I INCLUDE SIN AND GUILT, WHICH HAVE NO REMEDY BUT IN THEIR PLACE, AND EXCLUDE FIRSTBORN AND TITHE, WHICH CAN BE PROVIDED FOR ANYWHERE. ({SP_(77, 5, "שאין", "להם", "פרנסה", "אלא", "במקומם")} "which have no provision but in their place"): the inclusion and the restriction weighed by the offering\'s remedy — Mishnah Temurah 3:5 (the English); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(77, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'R. AKIVA: OF THE SUBSTITUTE OF HOLY THINGS THE VERSE SPEAKS — "YOU SHALL TAKE UP AND GO TO THE PLACE"; MIGHT EVEN THE FIRSTBORN AND TITHE? "AND YOUR VOWS." A SECOND ASSIGNMENT ({SP_(77, 6, "בתמורת", "קדשים", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of the substitute of holy things the verse speaks"): a DISPUTE on 12:26\'s subject — abroad (77:1) or the substitute (Leviticus 27:10, 33 — read at the valuations); 78:9-10 follow R. Akiva\'s reading. Fresh.')
srow(77, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT THE CATTLE TITHE APPLY IN PARTNERSHIP? "WHICH YOU (SINGULAR) HAVE." ({SP_(77, 7, "יכול", "יהא", "מעשר", "בהמה", "נוהג", "בשתפות")} "might the cattle tithe apply in partnership"): the singular suffix a PARAMETER. Fresh.')
srow(77, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT I EXCLUDE BROTHERS WHO ACQUIRED FROM THE ESTATE AND THEN DIVIDED? "WHICH YOU HAVE." ({SP_(77, 8, "האחים", "שקנו", "בתפוסת", "הבית")} "the brothers who acquired from the estate"): Mishnah Bekhorot 9:3 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(77, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'BEN AZZAI: MIGHT THE CATTLE TITHE APPLY TO AN ORPHAN\'S FLOCK? "ONLY." ({SP_(77, 9, "נוהג", "ביתום")} "apply to an orphan"): the restrictive "only" a fourth time (71:1, 71:5, 71:11, 76:2). Fresh.')

srow(78, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS, THE FLESH AND THE BLOOD" (12:27) — R. JOSHUA: IF THERE IS NO BLOOD THERE IS NO FLESH, AND IF NO FLESH NO BLOOD. The head row of piska 78 ({SP_(78, 1, "אם", "אין", "דם", "אין", "בשר")} "if there is no blood there is no flesh"): the pair "the flesh and the blood" read as mutual conditions — Tosefta Zevachim 4:1 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(78, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELIEZER: "THE BLOOD OF YOUR SACRIFICES SHALL BE POURED" — EVEN IF THERE IS NO FLESH. THEN WHAT DO I COMPARE IN "THE FLESH AND THE BLOOD"? FLESH TO BLOOD — AS THE BLOOD BY THROWING, SO THE FLESH BY THROWING. THE DISPUTE AND THE HEKESH ({SP_(78, 2, "אף", "על", "פי", "שאין", "בשר")} "even though there is no flesh"; {SP_(78, 2, "מה", "דם", "בזריקה", "אף", "בשר", "בזריקה")} "as blood by throwing, so flesh by throwing"): the juxtaposition (named by the row, "makkish") makes the flesh thrown onto the fire; Sifra Nedavah 4:12 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(78, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'MIGHT HE STAND AFAR AND THROW? "THE PRIEST SHALL ARRANGE THEM" (LEVITICUS 1:12) — HE STANDS NEAR AND ARRANGES ON THE PILE. ({SP_(78, 3, "עומד", "בקרוב", "וסודרם")} "he stands near and arranges them"): Leviticus 1 read (the ledger names 12:27). Fresh.')
srow(78, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM "THE PRIEST SHALL BURN THE WHOLE ON THE ALTAR" (LEVITICUS 1:9) — TO INCLUDE THE BONES, SINEWS, HORNS AND HOOVES; MIGHT IT BE EVEN IF THEY SEPARATED? "YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS, THE FLESH AND THE BLOOD." ({SP_(78, 4, "לרבות", "העצמות", "והגידים", "והקרנים", "והטלפים")} "to include the bones, the sinews, the horns and the hooves"): E1 (checked) from "the whole", restricted by 12:27\'s "flesh" — Mishnah Zevachim 9:5 (the English). Fresh.')
srow(78, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'OR "THE FLESH AND THE BLOOD" — MIGHT HE STRIP THE SINEWS AND BONES AND BRING UP THE FLESH? "THE WHOLE." HOW? ATTACHED — THEY ARE OFFERED; SEPARATED, EVEN ON THE ALTAR\'S TOP — THEY COME DOWN. ({SP_(78, 5, "מחברים", "יקרבו", "פרשו")} "attached, they are offered; separated"): Sifra Nedavah 6:9. Fresh.')
srow(78, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ALL HOLY THINGS REQUIRE AN APPLICATION AT THE BASE AND ONE POURING ON THE ALTAR? "YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS … AND THE BLOOD OF YOUR SACRIFICES SHALL BE POURED." ({SP_(78, 6, "מתן", "יסוד", "ושפיכה", "אחת")} "an application at the base and one pouring"): "shall be poured" — THE INK: the sin offering\'s verb (Leviticus 4:7, 18, 25, 30, 34, computed) said of every sacrifice\'s blood. Fresh.')
srow(78, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'WHENCE THAT THE TITHE AND THE PASSOVER, GIVEN IN ONE APPLICATION, ATONE? "YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS." ({SP_(78, 7, "שאם", "נתנם", "במתנה", "אחת", "כפר")} "that if he gave them in one application he atoned"). Fresh.')
srow(78, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'AND WHENCE THAT THE TITHE AND THE PASSOVER ARE GIVEN ONLY IN ONE APPLICATION? "THE BLOOD OF YOUR SACRIFICES SHALL BE POURED." ({SP_(78, 8, "שלא", "ינתנו", "אלא", "במתנה", "אחת")} "that they are given only in one application"): Tosefta Zevachim 6:15 (the English); Mishnah Zevachim 5:8 at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(78, 9, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ISHMAEL: OF THE SUBSTITUTE OF HOLY THINGS THE VERSE SPEAKS (12:26). ({SP_(78, 9, "בתמורת", "קדשים", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "of the substitute of holy things the verse speaks"): 77:6\'s reading in R. Ishmael\'s name — the Hebrew cites 12:26. Fresh.')
srow(78, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL TAKE UP AND GO TO THE PLACE" — HE HAS COME TO THE PLACE; WHAT SHALL HE DO WITH IT? "YOU SHALL OFFER YOUR BURNT OFFERINGS, THE FLESH AND THE BLOOD": AS THE BURNT OFFERING REQUIRES FLAYING, CUTTING AND WHOLE BURNING, SO ITS SUBSTITUTE; AS IT REQUIRES THE BASE AND ONE POURING, SO ITS SUBSTITUTE; AS ITS LIMBS THAT FLEW OFF THE ALTAR ARE RETURNED TO THE PILE, SO ITS SUBSTITUTE; AS ALL HOLY THINGS\' FLESH IS PERMITTED ONLY AFTER THE THROWING, SO THEIR SUBSTITUTES. THE SUBSTITUTE FOLLOWS ITS ORIGINAL ({SP_(78, 10, "אף", "תמורתה", "כיוצא", "בה")} "so its substitute is like it"): four rules copied from the original to the substitute — Mishnah Zevachim 9:6 (the English); 12:26-27 read as one sentence about the substitute (R. Akiva\'s and R. Ishmael\'s assignment). Fresh.')

srow(79, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"OBSERVE AND HEAR" (12:28) — IF YOU HEARD A LITTLE, YOU WILL HEAR MUCH; IF YOU KEPT A LITTLE, YOU WILL KEEP MUCH; IF YOU KEPT WHAT YOU HEARD, YOU WILL KEEP WHAT YOU HAVE NOT HEARD; KEEP WHAT IS IN YOUR HAND AND YOU WILL LEARN FOR THE FUTURE. The head row of piska 79 ({SP_(79, 1, "אם", "שמעת", "מעט", "סופך", "לשמוע", "הרבה")} "if you heard a little, your end is to hear much"): the two verbs read as a ladder of learning — Mekhilta Vayassa 1 (the English); 96:3 repeats it (the translator). Fresh.')
srow(79, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: ONE WHO MERITED TO LEARN TORAH MERITED FOR HIMSELF AND HIS GENERATIONS TO THE END OF ALL GENERATIONS. ({SP_(79, 2, "זכה", "לו", "ולדורותיו")} "he merited for himself and his generations"); no citation in either file; lacking in several manuscripts (the English). Fresh.')
srow(79, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"OBSERVE AND HEAR" — WHATEVER IS NOT IN THE CLASS OF LEARNING IS NOT IN THE CLASS OF DEED. ({SP_(79, 3, "כל", "שאינו", "בכלל", "משנה", "אינו", "בכלל", "מעשה")} "whatever is not in the class of learning is not in the class of deed"): 59:3-4\'s two nouns (mishnah, deed) bound — the deed depends on the learning. Fresh.')
srow(79, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"ALL THESE WORDS WHICH I COMMAND YOU" — THAT A LIGHT COMMANDMENT BE AS DEAR TO YOU AS A WEIGHTY ONE. ({SP_(79, 4, "שתהא", "מצוה", "קלה", "חביבה", "עליך", "כמצוה", "חמורה")} "that a light commandment be as dear to you as a weighty one"): Mishnah Avot 2:1 (the English); 82:1 again. Fresh.')
srow(79, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU DO THE GOOD AND THE RIGHT" — THE GOOD IN THE EYES OF HEAVEN, THE RIGHT IN THE EYES OF MAN: R. AKIVA; "HE SHALL FIND FAVOR AND GOOD UNDERSTANDING IN THE EYES OF GOD AND MAN" (PROVERBS 3:4); R. ISHMAEL: "THE RIGHT" IN THE EYES OF HEAVEN. THE PAIR DIVIDED ({SP_(79, 5, "הטוב", "בעיני", "שמים", "והישר", "בעיני", "אדם")} "the good in the eyes of Heaven and the right in the eyes of man"): a DISPUTE on the two adjectives (Tosefta Shekalim 2:1 — the English); THE INK: "the good and the right" 6:18 and 12:28 in the book, the Kings\' measure of a king (computed). Fresh.')

srow(80, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN THE LORD YOUR GOD CUTS OFF THE NATIONS" (12:29) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE CONTEXT, FOR AS ITS REWARD THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CUT OFF THE NATIONS. The head row of piska 80 ({SP_(80, 1, "עשה", "מצוה", "האמורה", "בענין", "שבשכרה")} "do the commandment said in the context, for as its reward"): the "when" clause read as a reward conditional (55:1\'s commonplace at 11:29 — the English; 75:1 the same at 12:20); THE INK: "when the LORD your God cuts off the nations" 12:29 and 19:1 (computed). Fresh.')
srow(80, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHITHER YOU GO TO DISPOSSESS THEM FROM BEFORE YOU" — AS THE REWARD OF COMING, YOU WILL DISPOSSESS. ({SP_(80, 2, "בשכר", "שתבוא", "תירש")} "as the reward that you come, you will dispossess"). Fresh.')
srow(80, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL DISPOSSESS THEM AND DWELL IN THEIR LAND" — FROM "YOU SHALL DWELL IN THEIR CITIES AND HOUSES" (19:1) MIGHT YOU NOT BE PERMITTED TO ADD TO THE BUILDING? "AND DWELL IN THEIR LAND" — WHEREVER YOU WISH TO BUILD, BUILD. ({SP_(80, 3, "כל", "מקום", "שאתה", "רוצה", "לבנות", "בנה")} "wherever you wish to build, build"): 19:1 (ahead) read against 12:29 — the land, not only the cities; 179:2 outside says it from 19:1\'s side. Fresh.')
srow(80, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL DISPOSSESS THEM AND DWELL" — R. JUDAH BEN BETERA, R. MATYA BEN HERESH, R. HANANIAH THE NEPHEW OF R. JOSHUA AND R. JONATHAN, GOING ABROAD, REACHED PALTOS AND REMEMBERED THE LAND; THEY WEPT, TORE THEIR GARMENTS AND READ "YOU SHALL POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT AND KEEP TO DO ALL THESE STATUTES" (11:31-32); THEY SAID: DWELLING IN THE LAND OUTWEIGHS ALL THE COMMANDMENTS. ({SP_(80, 4, "ישיבת", "ארץ", "ישראל", "שקולה", "כנגד", "כל", "המצוות", "שבתורה")} "dwelling in the Land of Israel is weighed against all the commandments in the Torah"): the story read at 12:29\'s dwelling — Ketubot 110b-111a at chapter 11\'s docket. Read before at chapter 11 (the ledger holds 80:4), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(80, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELAZAR BEN SHAMMUA AND R. YOHANAN THE SANDLER, GOING TO NISIBIS TO LEARN FROM R. JUDAH BEN BETERA, REACHED SIDON AND REMEMBERED THE LAND; THEY WEPT, TORE THEIR GARMENTS, READ THE VERSE (11:31-32), SAID DWELLING IN THE LAND OUTWEIGHS ALL THE COMMANDMENTS — AND TURNED BACK TO THE LAND. ({SP_(80, 5, "חזרו", "ובאו", "להם", "לארץ", "ישראל")} "they turned back and came to the Land of Israel"): the second story; Finkelstein doubts both original to the Sifrei (the English). Read before at chapter 11 (the ledger holds 80:5), REREAD WHOLE here.')

srow(81, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"TAKE HEED" (12:30) — A PROHIBITION; "LEST" — A PROHIBITION. The head row of piska 81 ({SP_(81, 1, "השמר", "בלא", "תעשה", "פן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "take heed — a prohibition; lest — a prohibition"): 70:1 and 74:6-7 a third time — the chapter\'s three "take heed" all prohibitions (the compile\'s three BLOCKs). Fresh.')
srow(81, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST YOU BE ENSNARED AFTER THEM" — LEST YOU BE DRAWN AFTER THEM, OR RESEMBLE THEM, DO AS THEY DO, AND THEY BECOME A SNARE TO YOU. ({SP_(81, 2, "שמא", "תמשך", "אחריהם")} "lest you be drawn after them"; {SP_(81, 2, "ויהיו", "לך", "למוקש")} "and they become a snare to you"): the rare niphal glossed by the common noun "snare" (7:16, 7:25\'s word — THE INK: the two snare roots, computed). Fresh.')
srow(81, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AFTER THEY ARE DESTROYED FROM BEFORE YOU" — WHY DO I DESTROY THEM? THAT YOU NOT DO AS THEY DID AND OTHERS COME AND DESTROY YOU (60:3 again). ({SP_(81, 3, "ויבואו", "אחרים", "וישמידו", "פניך")} "and others come and destroy you"). Fresh.')
srow(81, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST YOU INQUIRE AFTER THEIR GODS, SAYING" — DO NOT SAY: SINCE THEY GO OUT IN A TOGA, I TOO; IN PURPLE, I TOO; IN BROAD TROUSERS, I TOO — "AND I WILL DO SO TOO." ({SP_(81, 4, "הואיל", "והם", "יוצאים", "בטגא")} "since they go out in a toga"; {SP_(81, 4, "ואעשה", "כן", "גם", "אני")} "and I will do so, I too"): the inquiry read as the imitation of their dress — the loanwords of Rome (toga, purple) on the shelf; THE INK: 12:30\'s "saying" the chapter\'s one, the speaker\'s "I" the seeker\'s (computed). Fresh.')
srow(81, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT DO SO TO THE LORD YOUR GOD" (12:31) — THERE IS "SO" FOR THE SERVICE AND "SO" FOR THE THING SERVED. FROM HERE THEY SAID: WHAT IS OFFERED ON THE ALTAR, IF OFFERED TO AN IDOL — LIABLE; WHAT IS OFFERED TO AN IDOL, IF OFFERED ON THE ALTAR — EXEMPT; WHAT IS NOT OFFERED ON THE ALTAR, OFFERED TO AN IDOL — IF ITS LIKE IS OFFERED, LIABLE, IF NOT, EXEMPT. THE SINGULAR "SO" A DECISION TABLE ({SP_(81, 5, "בדבר", "שמקריבים", "אותו", "למזבח")} "regarding a thing that is offered on the altar"): the liability for idolatrous offering keyed to the Temple\'s own rite (Sanhedrin 60b-61a at 10b); THE INK: 12:4\'s plural and 12:31\'s singular the pair (computed). Fresh.')
srow(81, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT THEY NOT OFFER SIN AND GUILT OFFERINGS? "FOR EVERY ABOMINATION OF THE LORD WHICH HE HATES" — A THING HATED AND ABOMINABLE TO THE ALL-PRESENT. ANOTHER WORD: THEY INTENDED TO OFFER ONLY WHAT THE ALL-PRESENT HATES. "FOR EVEN THEIR SONS AND THEIR DAUGHTERS" — ONLY SONS AND DAUGHTERS? FATHERS AND MOTHERS WHENCE? "THEIR SONS" — EVEN THEIR SONS; "THEIR DAUGHTERS" — EVEN THEIR DAUGHTERS. R. AKIVA: I SAW A GENTILE WHO BOUND HIS FATHER BEFORE HIS DOG, AND IT ATE HIM. THE ABOMINATION\'S SCOPE ({SP_(81, 6, "דבר", "השנאוי", "ומתעב", "למקום")} "a thing hated and abominable to the All-Present"; {SP_(81, 6, "אבותם", "ואמותם", "מנין")} "their fathers and mothers whence"): E1 (checked) from "even" — the parents included; R. Akiva\'s witness the datum; THE INK: "which He hates" 12:31 and 16:22 alone; the children burned — Jeremiah 7:31\'s six shared tokens (computed). Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(77, r) for r in range(1, 10)] + [(78, r) for r in range(1, 11)] + [(79, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(80, r) for r in range(1, 6)] + [(81, r) for r in range(1, 7)], sorted(S)
